00:00:01.939 --> 00:00:03.530 align:start position:0%
final fantasy explorers is a mash-up of  final fantasy elements built within the  framework of creature tracking games  such as Monster Hunter the seemingly  endless march of quests can get  repetitive and tedious and the economy  is frustrating but it's fanservice at  its finest there's no real plot but  that's fine you're here to kill stuff  and the ability to swap job classes  whenever you want and test out all their  unique weapons and combat styles is a  delight it's like rerolling an MMO  character again and again without  penalty to your strengths progression  quest layouts can feel a bit samey but  it's worth grinding them out to get to  boss battles against giant Dolan's that  present some real tough tactical  challenges then there's the loop  defeating big baddies net too rare goods  and the more of you that team up in  multiplayer the more you'll get so you  can unlock that sweet sephiroth costume  and if you don't have friends you can  always summon an ally monster into  battle and make a cacti are chocobo  watch your back it's frustrating that  you have to pay in-game currency to  start some quests significantly  lightening your pockets when you're  saving harder and Gil for better  equipment but those big bad fights are  worth it final fantasy explorers isn't a  true Final Fantasy game in a sense but  it still hits the sweet spot by sending  you into a strange new world against  magnificent creatures and impossible  odds
 

